# Boarding House, flown from the Vestibule to the bell in the turret.
#
# The acceptance run for the port's second house, the way open-house.script is for its
# first. It starts where the house starts -- no `room` or `where` line, so the glider
# appears at the house's own `initial 32 112` in room 7 -- and it finishes by collecting
# the third and last star, which sets gameOver. See TestBoardingHouseCanBeFinished.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The route
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The house is 51 rooms; this route touches twelve of them, climbing five staircases and
# taking all three stars:
#
#   7  Vestibule     (f1 s55) -east-> 8  Front Hall  (f1 s56)  STAR
#                              -east-> 9  Mrs Ash's Parlour    -up->
#   20 First Landing (f2 s57) -east-> 21 Number One  (f2 s58)  -up->
#   30 Number Five   (f3 s58) -east-> 31 Music Room  (f3 s59)  STAR  -up->
#   38 Number Seven  (f4 s59) -east-> 39 Box Room    (f4 s60)  -up->
#   45 Water Tank    (f5 s60) -east-> 46 Tower Stair (f5 s61)  -up->
#   49 Bell Turret   (f6 s61) -- the third star, at frame 1447.
#
# Eleven rooms entered at 100 each plus three stars at 5,000 is 16,100, and the run ends
# with two mortals still in hand: nothing on this route can kill the glider, which is
# the point of a house whose interiors all follow one idiom.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Why the keystrokes alternate
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# levels/Boarding House.house.txt derives this at length and open-house.script derives
# it first, so the short version: the glide ratio is 5:3, two vents 216 px apart in a
# 512 px room are nowhere near the one-vent-per-100-px break-even, and holding the arrow
# down loses about 100 px of altitude per room. The glider has to stop in each column
# and let it carry it to the ceiling. Every `-` is a released right-arrow and every
# `right` is it pressed again.
#
# Three things about this house make its script shorter than its room count suggests.
#
# **The stair rooms need five events, not three.** MoveItUp fires on
# GliderInRect(112x32 at (H,28)) && !HeldRight, and GliderInRect is containment rather
# than overlap (internal/game/player/hitbox.go:55-58), so the whole 48x20 glider must
# fit: left in 336..400, top in 28..40. That band is *below* CeilingLimit 8, so a glider
# that has just ridden a vent to the ceiling is above the box and cannot be in it. The
# staircase is taken on the way back down, and the fifth event is that release: at f=390,
# 631, 872, 1113 and 1354, every one of them exactly 15 frames after the press that
# precedes it and every one at left 350, top 30.
#
# **Six legs begin with no keystroke.** The house's `initial 32 112` is inside room 7's
# own h 120 catchment, so the glider is lifted from frame 0 without being asked. And the
# walk out of a staircase ends at left 127, top 52 -- eleven frames of -4 px in V and
# -4 px in H from the left 171, top 96 it arrives at -- which is also inside the h 120
# catchment, so each of the five rooms entered by stairs starts the same way. That is
# why there are 46 events here and not 52.
#
# **The stars cost nothing.** All three sit at v 14 directly over a vent -- two at h 128
# and the turret's at h 336 -- so they are collected at the top of a ride the route was
# making anyway. Not one event below is spent on a prize.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Regenerating it
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# These frame numbers came out of the simulation, not out of arithmetic, and the reason
# is worth knowing before trying to recompute them: the hover cut-off is top = V-D-20 =
# 16, but the glider reaches it carrying VVel -6 against gravity's +3 per frame, so it
# coasts past and tops out between 6 and 10. All 23 presses below are at top 8, 9 or 10.
# A rule set written from the cut-off reproduces none of them.
#
# The rule set that does reproduce them, applied frame by frame against
# `glidertool replay -trace`, is four rules:
#
#   1. hold right;
#   2. release on the first frame the glider's left enters the catchment of the next
#      vent in this room it has not yet ridden -- left in [h-25, h+26] for a vent at h
#      -- and skip the release if nothing is held, because then the column already has
#      it;
#   3. press right on the first frame top <= 10;
#   4. in a room with a kUpStairs, after the second vent, release instead on the first
#      frame the glider is contained in the trigger box: left in [336,400] and top in
#      [28,40].
#
# A failure here is a flight-model change, and the room the trace stops in says which
# leg stopped working. It is not a house bug unless the house changed.

house Boarding House
seed 1
frames 1500
neighbors 9
players 1
sound off
clock 1994-10-14T10:09:00Z

# room 7, The Vestibule -- lifted off the h 120 vent with no keystroke, across to the
# h 336 one, then east out of the room.
at 21 right
at 61 -
at 82 right

# room 8, The Front Hall -- the h 120 vent, and the star at v 14 h 128 on the way up.
at 141 -
at 170 right
at 213 -
at 235 right

# room 9, Mrs Ash's Parlour -- h 120, then h 300, then down into the staircase box.
at 295 -
at 323 right
at 359 -
at 375 right
at 390 -

